{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/init(plan:limit:now:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/Failure"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Methods","anchor":"Type-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of Google Analytics 4’s Measurement Protocol, so an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a server can send events to a web or data stream’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/mp\/collect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder.swift#L101"},"modules":[{"name":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On macOS and Linux, make the destination with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, the stream’s API secret, this encoder and the Measurement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Protocol’s limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let googleAnalytics = try HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(","    measurementID: measurementID,  \/\/ the web or data stream's, G-…","    apiSecret: apiSecret,  \/\/ from the server's configuration, never an app's","    region: .global,  \/\/ or .eu, to have Google collect the data in the EU","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The encoder is for a server, and is compiled for macOS and Linux alone, as the Measurement","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Protocol takes none of its requests without the stream’s API secret, which must stay on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server: anyone holding it can send events to the property. A server forwarding an app’s events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remakes each ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the app’s identifier, timestamp and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and hands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them to the destination; tracking them again through a tracker with ","type":"text"},{"code":".sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every user as one ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request’s body is a JSON object of content type "},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holding one client’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events, oldest first, as the Measurement Protocol takes one "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" a request. A batch of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records from several sessions makes a request for each, in the order of each session’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record. The members are:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The records’ session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the first and last 64 bits of the UUID in decimal, joined by a period; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the same way when its context has no session, so each such record is a request of its own","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"consent","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ad_user_data"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ad_personalization"},{"text":", both ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DENIED"},{"text":", so Google uses none of the events for advertising","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One object per record: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":" as it is; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"params"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s stored properties by name; and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp_micros"},{"type":"text","text":", when it was tracked, in whole microseconds since 1970"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"params","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds "},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, the first 48 bits of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its version 7 "},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so Google Analytics groups the session’s events; it is left out for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session, or a session key of another version."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no user properties, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_location","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip_override","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_agent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so Google Analytics records no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"location or device for the events. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard context, and any other context value, aren’t sent. Google Analytics counts a user per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its users are sessions. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"engagement_time_msec","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent, as Traffluent doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measure engagement, so the events don’t count toward Google Analytics’ engagement time or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"engaged sessions, and its Realtime and Users reports can show no users while events arrive:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"check the event counts instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out. Google Analytics takes only strings, numbers and booleans as parameters, so an object or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array is spread into a parameter for each value it holds, named after its path joined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart_size"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags_0"},{"type":"text","text":"), and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", such as an optional without a value or a redacted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element of an array, is left out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event or parameter name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"breaks Google Analytics’ naming rules or is one it keeps for itself, one of more than 25","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameters, one with a string over 100 bytes, one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one that holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is more than 71 hours before or 15 minutes after the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch is encoded, or has no microseconds form, and one too large for a request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","isActive":true},{"text":"). ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":"s, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" logs and reports on its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"text":". Google Analytics would answer 2xx to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such an event and, under its default, relaxed validation, store it without the parameter that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"breaks a rule, or under a name it never checked. A Google Analytics 360 property takes values of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"up to 500 characters, but the encoder holds every property to the standard 100 bytes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Google Analytics takes an event up to 72 hours old; the encoder holds records to 71, the hour to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spare for the request to reach Google and for clocks that disagree. Each request’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EncodedRequest\/deadline"},{"type":"text","text":" is 71 hours after its oldest record was tracked, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops a request still being retried by then, every record of it, the younger ones included, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":", rather than send records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Google Analytics would store as 72 hours old."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol has no field that identifies an event, so Google Analytics counts each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one it receives: a record sent again, by a retry after Google stored it, by a delivery that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sends a cancelled batch again, or by a store’s redelivery after a relaunch, is counted twice. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record a store recovers keeps its session, so it is counted under the ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its first send.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits each client’s records into requests within the encoder’s limit,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for it. The Measurement Protocol answers 2xx to every request it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives, a malformed one or one whose events it doesn’t store included, so a record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder sends is counted as delivered whatever Google Analytics makes of it, and a wrong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measurement ID or API secret is answered 2xx with nothing stored: check the property’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Realtime event counts after setting the destination up. The bytes are the same for the same records,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the same time, on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their names’ UTF-8 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Events/documentation/Events/Sensitive":{"title":"Sensitive","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Sensitive"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Sensitive"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/events\/sensitive","abstract":[{"text":"A property value that a destination reads only through the record it arrived in, and not at all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once the record is redacted.","type":"text"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"BatchEncoder","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/s8SendableP"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/outcome(of:for:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Every 2xx answer counts as delivered: the Measurement Protocol answers 2xx to every request it receives, with no body that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"says whether it stored the events.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"outcome"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPTransportResponse","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations21HTTPTransportResponseV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"for"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EncodedRequest","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations14EncodedRequestV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ResponseOutcome","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15ResponseOutcomeO"}],"title":"outcome(of:for:)","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/outcome(of:for:)","type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/Failure":{"title":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder.Failure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Failure","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/Failure","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/failure","abstract":[{"text":"Why a record was left out of the batch’s requests.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder":{"role":"symbol","title":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"}],"url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Google Analytics 4’s Measurement Protocol, so an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" on a server can send events to a web or data stream’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/mp\/collect"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/requests(for:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","title":"requests(for:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"text":" as the requests the Measurement Protocol takes, a client’s records in each, within","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the encoder’s limit, with the records left out of them.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/requests(for:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"requests"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"for"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchRequests","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13BatchRequestsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0abC5ErrorO"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"batchLimit","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/batchlimit","abstract":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol’s limits on one request: 25 events and 100,000 bytes of body, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s included.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","role":"collection","title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"symbol","title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsencodingerror","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/init(plan:limit:now:)":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/init(plan:limit:now:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An encoder of the events "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" describes, splitting each batch to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"limit"},{"type":"text","text":", and leaving out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the records tracked too long before, or too far after, the time "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now"},{"type":"text","text":" gives."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifi